    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0361" n="349" sameAs="frus:frus1946v07/pg349"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24591/3–1146</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Deputy Director of
                        the Office of Near Eastern and African Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Allen</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-03-11">March 11, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Dr. Daftary<anchor n="10" xml:id="d258-f1"/> said that while the Iranian
                    Ambassador was proceeding on the assumption that Prime Minister Qavam will
                    remain entirely steadfast in prosecuting the Iranian case before the Security
                    Council, he wished to know whether the United States would be willing to
                    initiate an inquiry in the Council in case Qavam for any reason <pb facs="0362"
                        n="350" xml:id="pg350"/> felt unable to instruct his own representatives to
                    do so. Dr. Daftary recalled that at the last meeting of the Council, a
                    resolution was passed requesting USSR and Iran to report back to the Council the
                    result of their further negotiations. The Iranian Ambassador is anxious that
                    some one at the next meeting of the Council should call for this report. Since
                    Iran is not a member of the Council, it might be difficult for Iran either to
                    report or to call for a report, even assuming that Qavam remains anxious to
                    press the case.</p>
                <p>I assured Dr. Daftary that his request would be given due consideration in the
                    Department.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d258-f1" n="10" xml:id="d258-f1-content">
                <p>A. A. Daftary, Counselor of the Iranian Embassy.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
